"text":"Caring for a Sourdough Starter\n\nA sourdough starter is a living culture of wild yeast and bacteria. With a few minutes of attention each\nday, a healthy starter can leaven bread for years and develop a flavour that is uniquely yours.\n\nDaily feeding\nDiscard all but a small spoonful, then feed it equal weights of flour and lukewarm water. Stir well, cover\nloosely and leave it somewhere warm until it has doubled in size.\n\nUse unbleached flour whenever possible.\n\nFiltered water helps if your tap water is heavily chlorinated.\n\nKeep the jar away from direct sunlight.\n\nSigns of a healthy starter\nAlively starter smells pleasantly sour, is full of bubbles and rises predictably after each feeding.","conf":95.51724137931035,"languages":["eng"],"provider":"local","hasGeometry":true,"durationMs":679}